@startuml
!theme plain

title P3 Soundboard and Safe Automation Trigger Sequence

actor "User or Scoped Principal" as Actor
participant "Desktop UI or\nAuthenticated HTTPS API" as Surface
participant "Control API\n(primary + CAS/idempotency)" as Control
participant "Automation Runtime" as Runtime
participant "Cue/Schedule Store" as Store
participant "History/Audit" as History
participant "Transmission Service" as Tx
participant "Target Policy\nDND/Air/ACL" as Policy
participant "Desktop Targets" as Targets

== Configure ==
Actor -> Control: cue/schedule/feature CRUD\nor issue/revoke principal
Control -> Store: re-authorize primary inside writer\ncommit mutation + sanitized replay
Store --> Control: resource projection\nsecret only on first issue response
Control --> Actor: no-store response

note over Control,Runtime
  Scoped trigger is a generic 404 until the downstream
  runtime service is explicitly composed.
end note

== Trigger ==
Actor -> Surface: fire cue hotkey\nor scoped API trigger
Surface -> Runtime: request(trigger, cue, audience, delivery)
Runtime -> Store: load cue, principal,\nschedule and revoke state
Runtime -> Store: atomically claim occurrence\nor principal idempotency key
Store --> Runtime: one immutable execution\nor exact committed replay
Runtime -> Policy: validate scope, DND,\nquiet hours, Air policy,\nrate limits

alt Rejected
  Policy --> Runtime: denied(reason)
  Runtime -> History: audit denied event\nwith attribution
  Runtime --> Surface: reject(reason)
else Accepted
  Policy --> Runtime: allowed(target snapshot)
  Runtime -> Tx: create transmission\nfrom cue trigger
  Tx -> Targets: prepare / schedule / play
  Targets --> Tx: receipts and outcomes
  Tx -> History: status, receipts,\nattribution
  Runtime --> Surface: accepted(transmission id)
end

== Fast disable or revoke ==
Actor -> Surface: revoke token\nor disable schedule
Surface -> Runtime: revoke(principal)\nor disable(schedule)
Runtime -> Store: mark revoked/disabled
Runtime -> Store: query nonterminal executions\nby principal/schedule/feature/cue lineage
Runtime -> History: immutable audit entry

alt Later trigger arrives
  Surface -> Runtime: request(...)
  Runtime -> Store: load revoked state
  Runtime -> History: denied_revoked
  Runtime --> Surface: reject(revoked)
end

note over Runtime,Targets
  The runtime never opens microphone capture.
  It reuses cue-class media and standard delivery policy.
end note

@enduml
